COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.amazon_ads_targets_snapshot IS 'Sponsored Products product and auto targets (targeting clauses) with their current bid and state, one snapshot per load date. Grain: one row per (snapshot_date, target_id). Source: public.amazon_ads_targets_snapshot joined to the product of the ad group (analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products). Refresh: manual: python -m etl.amazon_dash_load --dir <folder of Data Dash pulls>; idempotent upsert on the natural key; not scheduled. Coverage: one snapshot (2026-11-12, 919 clauses: 696 enabled, 223 paused; 775 manual, 144 auto). Caveats: target_id equals keyword_id in the report tables. An auto target can have no bid of its own (it inherits the ad group default, which was not pulled). | product_slug is NULL for an ad group that advertises more than one product (product_resolution = ''mixed'') and for one with no product ad on file or no mapped ASIN (''unmapped''): count those rows as ''no single product'', never as a product.';
