COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.amazon_ads_campaigns_snapshot IS 'Sponsored Products campaigns with budget, bidding strategy and placement bid adjustments, one snapshot per load date. Grain: one row per (snapshot_date, campaign_id). Source: public.amazon_ads_campaigns_snapshot joined to the product of the ad group (analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products). Refresh: manual: python -m etl.amazon_dash_load --dir <folder of Data Dash pulls>; idempotent upsert on the natural key; not scheduled. Coverage: one snapshot (2026-11-13, 963 campaigns: 746 enabled, 217 paused). Caveats: Placement bid adjustments live here; Amazon has no placement performance report for these pulls, so the effect of a placement bid cannot be measured from this data. | A placement percentage that is NULL means the campaign sets no adjustment for it. | product_slug is NULL for an ad group that advertises more than one product (product_resolution = ''mixed'') and for one with no product ad on file or no mapped ASIN (''unmapped''): count those rows as ''no single product'', never as a product.';
