COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products IS 'Which product each Sponsored Products ad group advertises, from its product ads and the ASIN map: the product behind every keyword, search term and negative keyword row. Grain: one row per (campaign_id, ad_group_id) that has at least one product ad. Source: public.amazon_ads_product_ads joined to public.amazon_asin_products on the ASIN. Refresh: manual: python -m etl.amazon_dash_load --dir <folder of Data Dash pulls>; idempotent upsert on the natural key; not scheduled (the ASIN map is refreshed nightly by the feeds service). Coverage: 962 ad groups from the 2026-11-13 product ad snapshot. Caveats: An ad group that advertises ASINs of more than one product is ''mixed'' and has no product_slug: it is counted as no single product, not guessed. 31 of 962 ad groups were mixed on the first load. | An ad group in a report with no product ad on file is not in this view; the views that join it read it as ''unmapped''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products.campaign_id IS 'Campaign id (text).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products.ad_group_id IS 'Ad group id (text).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products.asins IS 'Distinct ASINs advertised in the ad group.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products.products IS 'Distinct products among those ASINs (ASINs with no product mapping are not counted).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products.product_slug IS 'vita-bull | beef-liver | boneflex | vita-belle | vital-flow when the ad group advertises one product; NULL when it advertises several (product_resolution ''mixed'') or none is mapped (''unmapped'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products.product_name IS 'Display name of product_slug; NULL when product_slug is NULL.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products.product_resolution IS 'single | mixed | unmapped: how the ad group''s product was found (product ads -> ASIN -> amazon_asin_products).';
COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic IS 'Paid search terms (Sponsored Products) next to the organic Search Query Performance numbers of the same term, product and week: what you pay for against how much of that search you win. Grain: one row per (week_start, product_slug, search_term_key); product_slug NULL = an ad group with no single product. Source: public.amazon_ads_search_term_daily + analytics.amazon_ads_ad_group_products + public.amazon_sqp_weekly (US). Refresh: manual: python -m etl.amazon_dash_load --dir <folder of Data Dash pulls>; idempotent upsert on the natural key; not scheduled (the organic side is refreshed nightly by the feeds service). Coverage: paid side from 2026-09-09; organic columns only where Amazon listed the term for the product that week (about the top 100 terms per product per week). Caveats: week_start is a Sunday: Amazon''s Search Query Performance week (Sunday to Saturday), not an ISO (Monday) week, so paid days and organic weeks line up exactly. The first and last paid weeks can be partial. | Organic columns are NULL (not zero) when Amazon did not list the term that week: absence only means it was outside the top terms. has_organic_row says which. | Search Query Performance market totals are the MAX over the ASIN rows of a term-week and our counts the SUM; shares are recomputed here, percent 0 to 100. Our impressions, clicks and purchases include sponsored placements, so they overlap the paid columns: do not add paid and organic. | A paid row with no single product reads all products together in the organic columns (organic_scope = ''all products'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.week_start IS 'Sunday that starts the Search Query Performance week.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.product_slug IS 'vita-bull | beef-liver | boneflex | vita-belle | vital-flow when the ad group advertises one product; NULL when it advertises several (product_resolution ''mixed'') or none is mapped (''unmapped'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.product_name IS 'Display name of product_slug; NULL when product_slug is NULL.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.product_resolution IS 'single | mixed | unmapped: how the ad group''s product was found (product ads -> ASIN -> amazon_asin_products).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.search_term_key IS 'Normalised search term (lower case, whitespace collapsed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.impressions IS 'Paid impressions of the week.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.clicks IS 'Paid clicks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.cost IS 'Paid cost, US dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.purchases_7d IS 'Paid purchases, 7-day attribution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.sales_7d IS 'Paid sales, 7-day attribution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.organic_scope IS 'product (the organic columns read that product''s rows) | all products (the paid row has no single product).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.search_volume IS 'Amazon searches for the term that week (market total); NULL when not listed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.our_impression_share IS 'Our impressions / all impressions for the term, percent 0-100 (includes our sponsored placements).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.our_click_share IS 'Our clicks / all clicks for the term, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.our_cart_add_share IS 'Our cart adds / all cart adds, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.our_purchase_share IS 'Our purchases / all purchases for the term, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.our_clicks IS 'Our clicks on the term in Search Query Performance (organic and sponsored).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.our_purchases IS 'Our purchases of the term in Search Query Performance (search-origin, same day).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_ads_search_terms_vs_organic.has_organic_row IS 'True when Search Query Performance has a row for this term, product scope and week.';
